The full GSE201623 RNA audit covers 17,949 numeric genes using the exact inherited source-preserving Parquet. The fresh gzip decompressed hash matches b3d15fe88a6a680290cb57a382ac93c9f5451966d5d20b58bfa2994b0ddcb580. Egr2 rises and Jun falls in every pairwise AS/GFP comparison; Pmp22 is 0.885x. A broad ranking exposed AS2-specific hemoglobin enrichment. The refined ten-gene counts are 953, 259574, 620, 462; excluding those genes leaves the target ratios. The preliminary broad globin substring files include non-hemoglobin names; use the registered rna-hemoglobin outputs. No raw-read origin was inferred. GEO GSNAP versus paper HISAT2 remains a provenance discrepancy, and RNA libraries cannot be matched to the protein assay cultures.

Primary full texts and native supplements were acquired with verified TLS. XML HTTP500 responses were handled through actual PMC HTML for TEAD, enhancer, miR29, original 2017 Egr2-AS and lipid papers. Exact selected passages and an assay table are preserved. The 2017 nuclear-run-on and transient injury effects narrow the interpretation but do not settle the later RNA discrepancy. The linked 2017 supplemental PDF returned HTML; EuropePMC returned a non-open-access error XML despite HTTP200. Those bytes are preserved as failures, not valid PDF/ZIP. The 2024 native nested PDFs were inspected through locally authored Swift/PDFKit extraction. The miR29 source has r-squared 0.78 in Results versus 0.078 in the caption; that discrepancy remains unresolved. Nerve pools and technical repeats were not treated as independent animals.

Independent quantitative ATAC uses deposited unzoomed TDF tracks, not raw sequencing. read_tdf.py checks binary structure and tile consumption. An initial strict positive-width assertion exposed zero-width bed intervals; allowing them with zero integral preserves their meaning. Missing intervals are not zeros. The embedded track normalization is ten million tags; mm10 is sourced from GEO/paper, not the local-path genome field. Across 33,105 promoter/site windows, 3,288 pass 90% observed coverage in both tracks. Common-base Pmp22 log2 differences are -0.447, -0.626 and -0.718; the reported RUNX site is -0.111 and the broader promoter median about -0.450. With one library per genotype and differing DRG/tumor annotations, no causal differential-accessibility inference is made. Source Figure5 already describes lower P2 accessibility with higher P1 RNA. Contemporary RefSeq windows were not guessed to be P1/P2.

The consequential RUNX RNA follow-up analyzed all 24,062 gene rows in six processed count files. Pmp22 is 2.308x, Mpz 2.820x, and Mbp 2.475x, with all nine cross-group pairwise increases. Nf803/Nf809 and Rx1692/Rx1698 GEO titles are swapped relative to filenames and internal headers, but stay within groups. GEO omits Nf1 from the Rx genotype field while the paper describes triple knockout. No cross-assay pairing or clean genotype causality is justified. The gene matrix cannot reproduce Kallisto transcript estimates. All-NaN pairwise warnings arise from zero denominators and are preserved as NA; Arrow sysctl warnings are environmental. No fresh DE p-values were made.

The protein analysis used all 670 selected XLSX entries, 515 unique proteins and 40 shared by all three variant lists. No workbook formulas were executed, no unlisted values were zero-filled, and differences of enrichments were not assigned fresh p-values. LMAN1 binding versus knockout response, and functional UGGT1 despite screen absence, distinguish interaction from necessity. The PXD023091 SEARCH files exceed the per-file cap; no small replicate-channel matrix was listed and no raw processing was attempted. The G3BP analysis uses published half-life summaries and TableS2: 4.4 hours control versus 4.2 after siG3BP1, in MCF7 cells rather than Schwann cells.

The human analysis covers 43,931 probes from 12 arrays representing seven donors. BAR duplication and JIM L16P are one donor each, with technical duplicates averaged within donor. Log10 test/reference semantics were verified in complete source sample tables. The two PMP22 probe contrasts are 25.6x/2.66x for BAR and 27.4x/4.86x for JIM. They were neither assigned P1/P2 labels nor combined into a dosage coefficient. The broad BAR/JIM contrast correlation is 0.812; state, tissue and donor effects remain confounded.

